[# decorative/corner-accent: a section framed by an accent-colored corner (top and left edges, or top and right).

   Made from section borders, so there are no images. The corner is drawn on the section's own border, which
   keeps the content aligned.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: borders on the section table are honored.
   - Gmail apps: fine.
   - Dark mode: the section background swaps via dm-* classes when on the brand surface, the accent border stays. #]
<mj-section[[ cc(dm(s.background, 'bg'), cls) ]] background-color="[[ s.background ]]" padding="[[ s.padding ]]" border-top="[[ s.thickness ]] solid [[ s.color ]]"[% if s.corner == 'left' %] border-left="[[ s.thickness ]] solid [[ s.color ]]"[% else %] border-right="[[ s.thickness ]] solid [[ s.color ]]"[% endif %]>
  <mj-column>
    [[ data.content ]]
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
